  <diagram id="iE1qgISvgQB8wLEqIJYx" name="3-Questions-Assumptions">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1194" dy="718" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="0" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="pkUwpQWtBuZXsa4fr1_h-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&#xa;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;QUESTIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q1 — Section 7.1: Branch Manager History&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Should the system store the start and end dates of every manager&#39;s assignment to a branch, including previous managers?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q2 — Section 7.1: Employee Supervision&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Can an employee supervise multiple employees, and are there any restrictions on who can act as a supervisor?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q3 — Section 7.2: Training Attempts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Should an employee&#39;s training result be recorded only after completing the course, and what defines a passing score?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q4 — Section 7.3: Vehicle Models and Categories&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;What unique identifier should be assigned to each vehicle model and category, since the SRS does not specify their IDs?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q5 — Section 7.3: Luxury Vehicle Pricing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Can a vehicle have its own daily rate in addition to its category rate, and which rate takes priority when calculating rental charges?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q6 — Section 7.3: Price History&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;How should the system handle overlapping or consecutive validity periods for category and vehicle prices?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q7 — Section 7.4: Extra Price History&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Should the system maintain a separate historical price list for extras, in addition to storing the price charged on each rental?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q8 — Section 7.5: GPS Devices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Is the SIM card number unique for every GPS device, and can a device be removed or reinstalled in another vehicle?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q9 — Section 7.7: Customer Identification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Must an individual customer provide exactly one identification number: a national ID or a passport number?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q10 — Section 7.7: Authorized Drivers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;When an authorized corporate driver is also an individual customer, should both records be linked to identify the same person?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q11 — Section 7.7: Blacklist History&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Can a customer be blacklisted more than once, and can a blacklist decision later be reversed?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q12 — Section 7.8: Corporate Contracts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Can a corporate contract contain multiple category discounts with different validity periods, and can multiple contracts for the same company overlap?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q13 — Section 7.9: Promotion Usage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Does a promotion count as used when a reservation is created, confirmed, or when the rental is completed?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q14 — Section 7.10: Loyalty Points&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;What are the exact rules for calculating earned and redeemed points, and can redeemed points cause a customer&#39;s balance to become negative?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q15 — Section 7.10: Loyalty Tier&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Are loyalty tiers calculated using the customer&#39;s current points balance, and do redeemed points affect the customer&#39;s tier immediately?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q16 — Section 7.12: Additional Drivers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Should additional drivers be identified as individual customers, authorized corporate drivers, or can they be stored without linking them to existing customer records?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q17 — Section 7.12: Individual Main Driver&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;For individual rentals, must the main driver always be the customer who rented the vehicle?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q18 — Section 7.13: Insurance Price History&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Should historical insurance package prices be stored in a separate price-history table, in addition to the price charged on each rental?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q19 — Section 7.15: Supplier Identification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;What unique identifier should be assigned to each supplier, since the SRS only specifies the supplier&#39;s name, phone number, and email?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q20 — Section 7.16: Corporate Invoices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Should corporate invoices be represented as separate database entities, and what information should each monthly invoice contain?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q21 — Section 7.16: Payment References&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Can a payment reference be mandatory for card and bank transfer payments while remaining empty for cash payments?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&#xa;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="960" width="750" x="40" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pkUwpQWtBuZXsa4fr1_h-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&#xa;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;ASSUMPTIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A1 — Section 7.1: Employee and Branch Identifiers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;EmployeeID and BranchCode are treated as unique primary identifiers, as described in the SRS.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A2 — Section 7.2: Training Attempts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Each training attempt is uniquely identified by the combination of EmployeeID, CourseCode, and AttemptNo.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A3 — Section 7.3: Category and Model Identifiers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;CategoryID and ModelID are assumed to be generated unique identifiers because the SRS does not specify their formats.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A4 — Section 7.3: Vehicle Status History&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;A separate status history record is maintained for each vehicle status change, including the employee and timestamp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A5 — Section 7.3: Luxury Vehicle Pricing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Vehicle-specific price history is used to represent special daily rates for luxury vehicles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A6 — Section 7.5: GPS Installation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;A GPS device may remain uninstalled in the warehouse. VIN and InstallationDate are both empty when the device is not installed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A7 — Section 7.6: Transfer Identifier&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;TransferID is assumed to be a generated unique identifier for each vehicle transfer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A8 — Section 7.7: Authorized Drivers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;DriverNumber is unique only within its corporate customer, so the combination of CustomerNumber and DriverNumber identifies an authorized driver.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A9 — Section 7.7: Blacklist Records&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;A customer may have multiple blacklist records over time. Each record is identified by the customer and the blacklist date.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A10 — Section 7.8: Corporate Contracts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;ContractID is assumed to be a generated unique identifier for each corporate contract.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A11 — Section 7.10: Loyalty Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Each points movement has its own generated TransactionID. The current loyalty tier is determined from the points balance rather than entered manually.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A12 — Section 7.11: Reservations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;A reservation may be linked to at most one rental. Walk-in rentals do not require a reservation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A13 — Section 7.12: Rental Drivers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;A rental has one main driver, represented according to the customer&#39;s type. Additional drivers are recorded separately for each rental.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A14 — Section 7.13: Rental Insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;The price charged for each selected insurance package is stored in the rental insurance record to preserve the historical rental price.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A15 — Section 7.14: Damage Reports&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;ReportNumber is unique within its rental, and a damage report is identified by RentalNumber and ReportNumber.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A16 — Section 7.14: Feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;A rental can have at most one feedback record.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A17 — Section 7.15: Supplier Identification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;SupplierID is assumed to be a generated unique identifier because the SRS does not specify a supplier primary key.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A18 — Section 7.15: Supplier and Part Relationship&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;The combination of SupplierID and PartNumber identifies each supplier-part relationship.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;A19 — Section 7.16: Payments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;Each payment belongs to exactly one rental, and a rental may have multiple payments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&#xa;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1000" width="740" x="50" y="1020" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pkUwpQWtBuZXsa4fr1_h-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&#xa;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;CONTRADICTIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;C1 — Section 8: Stakeholder Interview Notes vs Section 9: NFR-1 Performance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 8: The Head of Branch Operations states that rental check-out should take no more than &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;3 minutes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Section 9 (NFR-1): Rental check-out must complete in under &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;3 seconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; of system time.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Contradiction:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; The two requirements specify different checkout time limits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;Resolution Required:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt; Confirm the intended performance target with the business stakeholders. The 3-second requirement may refer to system processing time, while the 3-minute requirement may refer to the complete counter operation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&#xa;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="750" width="750" x="45" y="1754" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
